\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\i0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Allows the delegate to constrain the 
\i y
\i0  coordinate limits of a divider when the user drags the mouse. This method is invoked before the NSSplitView begins tracking the mouse to position a divider. When this method is invoked, the limits have already been set and are stored in 
\i min
\i0  (the topmost limit) and 
\i max
\i0  (the bottommost limit). You may further constrain the limits by setting the variables indicated by 
\i min
\i0  and 
\i max
\i0 , but you cannot extend the divider limits. 
\i min
\i0  and 
\i max
\i0  are specified in the NSSplitView's flipped coordinate system. The divider to be repositioned is indicated by 
\i offset
\i0 , an index that counts the dividers from top to bottom starting with divider 0.\

\fs14 \

